WEBVTT

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:22.122
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.697
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.301
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:43.343
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:54.117
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.558
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.996
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.067
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:14.735
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.796
Pops...

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.970
A blue astral eye...

00:01:55.815 --> 00:02:00.684
The Blue Astral Eye

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.799
We should get going right away.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.393
The Inspection Force could be
about to make another move.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.736
Maybe.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.794
She has no external injuries.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.403
Zankan probably got her out in time.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:24.077
I don't think moving will
be a physical strain on her.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.375
No, not until she regains consciousness.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.314
You'll want to say goodbye
to your father, right?

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.027
Millie's mother...

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:51.932
...was killed by the Inspection Force
when she was still little.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.208
She got caught in a Technos Taboo raid.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.078
Was it Blue Breaker?

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:01.804
Nope.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.282
Just the normal Inspection Force.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.455
The people they were dealing with
apparently panicked and opened fire.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.594
That led to a shootout,
and she got hit by a stray bullet.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.395
I guess it was bad luck, really.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.851
This was bad luck, too.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.821
I was right there!

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.321
And yet...

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.865
I couldn't... do anything!

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.405
I guess Millie's seen my astral eye now.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.751
About that astral eye...

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.150
It's a different color, right?

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.884
I didn't make the cut.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:19.188
The astral eye is a physical
characteristic of The Third.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.661
Also the source of their name,

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:25.324
the crimson third eye is
embedded in their foreheads.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.468
Through their astral eyes,

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:32.038
they have the ability to directly
access various computer systems...

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.871
...and process information.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:39.105
Check data. Honoka. The Third.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.508
Registration number: NMT-0103.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.313
Individual name: Honoka. Show image.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.721
Kway response: Negative.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:54.250
FBD: Negative. AVS: Negative.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:55.657
Classify.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.489
She is not one of The Third.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.868
Right after I was born,

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:05.133
I was taken to Hyperius, The Third's city.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.940
But I got sent home right away.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.736
Right away?

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.307
Because I didn't make the cut.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.378
Even though I have the astral eye,

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.313
without any of The Third's abilities,
they had no use for me.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.675
That's all there was to it, both for them and me.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:22.651
But the stickler was that I was born
in a village out in the boondocks.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.189
I mean, think about it.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.949
There was nothing around there.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.988
There was apparently quite the
commotion when I was born.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.537
With a member of The Third from the village,

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:40.131
they figured their lives
should become a little better.

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:43.274
But in the end, I turned out to
be just a might-have-been.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.745
Considering they had big expectations,

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:48.373
I imagine their sense of disappointment
was pretty huge, too.

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:51.417
They'd thought they could finally say goodbye...

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.942
...to their harsh and fruitless way of life,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.457
but in the end, their rejoicing was premature.

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:59.789
But you are not responsible for that.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.186
No, I'm not.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:04.357
But it's not like I can't understand.

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.966
I've lived here on the frontier, too,

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:11.630
and I think I understand some of the
hardships of making a life out here.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.105
No, that's not true...

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.402
I've been pretty blessed.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:17.367
What?

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.606
I was raised in a caravan.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.813
Grandpa took me in when I was still a baby.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.316
Grandpa?

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.945
Well, I call him that,
but he's not my real grandpa.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:32.856
Walken...

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:35.057
The man who raised me.

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.698
No child-rearing expenses are necessary.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:42.068
In fact, she is to be an
official member of the caravan,

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.070
so I will pay you for her contract.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.672
Naturally, whenever we pass near this village,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.232
I promise that she will be sent to visit you.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.311
We do not want money or anything else.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:55.178
As long as this child... As long
as Honoka grows up healthy.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.215
We live in a small world.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.286
If she stayed here,

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:03.449
Honoka will surely never be free
of the mark on her forehead.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:08.760
This is the best way for us
to lift that curse from her.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:13.065
We have but one wish.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.059
That this child... That Honoka be happy.

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.737
That is all.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.170
I promise you.

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:22.432
I will raise this child with all due responsibility.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.443
Not that I remember any of this.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:29.103
I was still a baby then.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.679
It's all stuff I heard from Grandpa.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.912
Have you been in contact
with your parents since?

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.450
Because I didn't make the cut,

00:07:36.923 --> 00:07:39.619
I think they both faced all sorts of hardships.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:44.588
Grandpa took me in to the caravan
because he understood that situation.

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:00.273
Do you see them, Honoka?

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:07.885
It's string! Pieces of string are jumping!

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:10.012
Those are sand dragons.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.420
Sand ragons?

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.150
Sand "dragons."

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:17.622
Giant worms that traverse the desert.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.693
Look at them closely so you don't forget.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.628
Sand ragons!

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:26.803
Life in the caravan suited me.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:30.142
I got to go to all sorts of places
and meet all sorts of people,

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:31.871
and I never once felt lonely.

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:37.413
I was able to feel that was my home, my family.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:43.354
So, this time, I'm hoping
I can be Millie's caravan.

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:48.560
But I'd been keeping this
hidden at Grandpa's advice.

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:52.297
Not surprisingly, when I was a kid,
I didn't understand why I should.

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:56.400
But in the end, I'm not one of
The Third, nor am I like everyone else.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:59.663
There's no way for me to change that fact.

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.266
Did Mr. Zankan not know, either?

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:06.679
He did. My old friends from
the caravan all know.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:08.146
But with Millie...

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:11.382
Her mother was killed by
the Inspection Force, so...

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.686
And I never found the right time to tell her.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:14.948
She might hate me now.

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:19.358
I wonder if she thinks I'm with The Third now...

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.426
Honoka, Millie has regained consciousness.

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:23.560
Millie has?!

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:28.033
Millie...

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:41.141
Right then, Honoka remembered that
she was not wearing her bandana.

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:44.576
There was no need to hide anything anymore.

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:48.984
But in that moment,
Honoka could only stand there.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.091
STW-9000.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:59.629
I am here to question you regarding
your latest combat data record.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.170
You were attacked by an individual
by the name of "Honoka".

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.138
What was the nature of this attack?

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.541
It was an attack that the
sensors could not detect.

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:09.675
Be specific.

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:12.912
A physical contact that did
not possess kinetic force.

00:10:12.912 --> 00:10:14.213
Were you able to pick it up?

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:14.645
No.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:15.711
Moving on then.

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:18.417
Why did you withdraw in
the middle of your mission?

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:19.941
I am not authorized.

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:22.051
What do you mean?

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:24.757
I am not authorized to injure the target,

00:10:24.757 --> 00:10:27.123
otherwise known as the individual "Honoka".

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.761
In conducting my missions,

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:31.564
I was instructed that this
was my highest priority.

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.499
From whom? For what purpose?

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:35.701
The order was issued by
Council of The Third...

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:37.692
...standing member Joganki.

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:41.165
Both the purpose and meaning of this
non-aggression order are unknown.

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:43.307
Joganki...

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:18.371
She wanted to say something to her.

00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:22.678
She wanted to hold her tight
and ease her heartache.

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:27.715
But right then, Honoka found
herself unable to do anything.

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:33.386
Honoka, we've put more than
enough distance between us.

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:35.652
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:38.725
I'm just... having a hard
time finding the resolve...

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:42.101
But it'd be Pops who'd be most upset...

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:45.628
...if it got raided by wanderers
or the Inspection Force...

00:11:46.639 --> 00:11:47.936
Bogie, ignite it.

00:11:58.484 --> 00:12:00.952
Goodbye, Pops.

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.021
Emporium?

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:14.629
Yeah.

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:16.801
Pops' younger sister is there.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:20.004
I think it'll be best for Millie to live with her.

00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:23.439
I want to be with her, but there's
just no way, you know?

00:12:23.676 --> 00:12:25.200
Perhaps so.

00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:27.244
I'm heartless, aren't I?

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:29.414
It is a sensible decision.

00:12:30.282 --> 00:12:33.774
It cannot be an easy thing to raise a child.

00:12:41.527 --> 00:12:42.494
Iks?

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:50.864
Oh, that's okay. I'll do that later.

00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:52.267
You can just take it easy, Millie.

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:55.039
Dust is the natural enemy of machines...

00:12:55.207 --> 00:12:57.141
That's what Father always said...

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:01.037
Say, Millie...

00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:02.777
What?

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:08.144
Well, don't worry about being
too thorough with that.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.045
Okay.

00:13:26.205 --> 00:13:28.730
Those of The Third are mutants.

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:32.672
And Honoka is a mutant among The Third.

00:13:33.179 --> 00:13:36.205
Both her powers and her blue astral eye...

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:38.575
...can be explained away
when thought of that way.

00:13:39.485 --> 00:13:42.818
That troublesome visitor accompanied
by that troublesome girl,

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:45.420
not to mention Joganki's
non-aggression order...

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:52.796
It seems a somewhat forcible method
will be necessary to separate them.

00:14:05.811 --> 00:14:07.244
I'm done.

00:14:31.437 --> 00:14:33.667
Please do not be too hard on yourself.

00:14:34.173 --> 00:14:35.663
It was not your fault.

00:14:36.342 --> 00:14:38.867
It was entirely out of your hands.

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:40.506
There are a ton of things...

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:43.538
There are a ton of things I want to do.

00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:45.351
I can't forgive Blue Breaker.

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:46.919
I want to avenge Zankan.

00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:48.854
I want to ease Millie's suffering.

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:50.549
I want to make Millie happy.

00:14:53.492 --> 00:14:54.356
But...

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.522
There isn't a thing I can do right now.

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.122
I can't do anything for Millie.

00:15:01.867 --> 00:15:02.856
Miss Honoka...

00:15:07.306 --> 00:15:08.102
Thank you.

00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:12.071
Your being here has helped a lot.

00:15:12.211 --> 00:15:14.046
If it were just Millie and me,

00:15:14.046 --> 00:15:16.947
I think I really wouldn't know what to do.

00:15:27.326 --> 00:15:28.918
I might've found something good.

00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:30.986
But I don't see anything.

00:15:31.363 --> 00:15:32.455
I can hear it.

00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:39.768
Father...

00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:48.914
I don't know if it's because of this
or not, but I can hear things.

00:15:48.914 --> 00:15:51.348
Like the voices of the stars,
and the song of the desert and wind.

00:15:52.818 --> 00:15:55.412
And even the rumblings
of mist duck stomachs.

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:02.322
I've always wanted to fly.

00:16:02.661 --> 00:16:05.425
It'd be so nice if I could get to higher places.

00:16:05.831 --> 00:16:08.061
If I were one of The Third,

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.704
I'd use all the knowledge and
technology they've hoarded away,

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:14.106
and I'd fly, even beyond the skies.

00:16:14.106 --> 00:16:17.598
Does that mean that you actually
wanted to be one of The Third?

00:16:18.277 --> 00:16:21.178
No, no. I can say these things because I don't.

00:16:21.413 --> 00:16:23.382
If I really were one of The Third,

00:16:23.382 --> 00:16:27.148
I'd probably be spending my time on
stupid things like that idiot Joganki.

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:28.647
Such as his courtship of you?

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.311
Oh, please!

00:16:30.689 --> 00:16:34.216
What he wants isn't me, it's my power.

00:16:35.194 --> 00:16:35.922
Power?

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:37.687
I'll show you.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.990
There's no point in hiding it anyway.

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:43.765
Hold this for a sec.

00:16:45.404 --> 00:16:48.066
Kind of between your thumb and forefinger.

00:16:48.173 --> 00:16:49.640
And hold it out.

00:16:50.943 --> 00:16:51.637
Like this?

00:16:55.247 --> 00:16:55.645
Okay.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.382
Done.

00:17:08.794 --> 00:17:09.928
This is...

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:11.897
Grandpa told me that it's chi.

00:17:11.897 --> 00:17:14.900
That it's an energy all beings
have and stuff like that,

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.402
but the theoretical stuff is beyond me.

00:17:16.402 --> 00:17:17.892
I'm all about practical experience.

00:17:18.303 --> 00:17:21.073
And using a sword as a conduit came
from practical experience as well?

00:17:21.073 --> 00:17:22.438
You got it.

00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:24.839
It's easier for me to visualize that way.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:28.607
When I don't have anything, it can
come out like a lump sometimes.

00:17:29.615 --> 00:17:31.383
Oh, I just heard it again!

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:32.475
The "something good?"

00:17:32.584 --> 00:17:33.812
It's close.

00:17:34.153 --> 00:17:35.916
You still won't tell me?

00:17:36.121 --> 00:17:37.918
It's best to see it with your own eyes.

00:17:38.791 --> 00:17:41.589
STW-9000, you have a mission.

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:42.785
Prepare to move out!

00:17:49.268 --> 00:17:50.200
What's wrong?

00:17:59.845 --> 00:18:00.743
We're here.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.238
This place?

00:18:08.387 --> 00:18:09.854
But there's nothing here...

00:18:10.556 --> 00:18:12.421
Listen closely.

00:18:13.025 --> 00:18:14.014
Like this?

00:18:31.677 --> 00:18:32.575
Trnkas.

00:18:32.945 --> 00:18:36.472
A legendary flower that blooms
at night and wilts by dawn.

00:18:36.715 --> 00:18:40.219
It's a sight you rarely get to see,
even if you live out in the desert.

00:18:40.219 --> 00:18:42.054
This is only the third time
I've seen them myself.

00:18:42.054 --> 00:18:43.385
How splendid...

00:18:43.956 --> 00:18:46.754
So you sensed the vital
energy of these flowers...

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:51.455
For Millie?

00:18:51.563 --> 00:18:53.690
Yeah, I want to show it to her.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.258
I'm sure she'll like it.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.895
Grandpa often told me...

00:18:59.438 --> 00:19:02.601
There's a limit to what you
can do while you're alive.

00:19:02.975 --> 00:19:04.510
No matter how hard you try,

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:07.679
you won't be able to do even one
one-hundredth of what you want to do.

00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:09.615
So he told me I should take each moment...

00:19:09.615 --> 00:19:12.015
...and do my best to accomplish
whatever I could.

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:15.384
This is the best I can do for Millie right now.

00:19:17.523 --> 00:19:19.821
I heard about the incident in Emporium.

00:19:20.259 --> 00:19:24.355
You apparently tried to abduct
the visitor, Iks, by force?

00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:26.054
You make it sound so scandalous.

00:19:26.431 --> 00:19:28.834
I thought it would be better
to take him someplace...

00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:30.893
...where we could at least keep an eye on him.

00:19:31.737 --> 00:19:33.839
Is that why you have asked me...

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:36.330
...to rescind my non-aggression
order regarding Honoka?

00:19:37.609 --> 00:19:41.272
You find the girl accompanying
the visitor to be a hindrance?

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.778
When taking into consideration
the worst-case scenario.

00:19:44.383 --> 00:19:46.251
Do you intend to use him, too?

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:46.945
Yes.

00:19:47.152 --> 00:19:49.279
I can't say your methods are very tasteful.

00:19:49.354 --> 00:19:51.490
When her abilities are
taken into consideration,

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.754
I believe it is the most logical choice.

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:58.389
Or is there a reason you do not wish
to allow her to come under attack?

00:19:59.364 --> 00:20:00.228
No.

00:20:00.732 --> 00:20:02.700
Then I trust there is no problem.

00:20:03.135 --> 00:20:06.434
Please take care of the matter regarding
the non-aggression order.

00:20:14.513 --> 00:20:17.880
You've caught the attention of a
troublesome opponent, Honoka.

00:20:22.454 --> 00:20:24.149
Millie!

00:20:26.725 --> 00:20:27.885
Hono...

00:20:29.795 --> 00:20:31.126
Millie!

00:20:32.331 --> 00:20:32.820
What?

00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:35.634
Millie?

00:20:35.634 --> 00:20:37.067
Where were you?!

00:20:38.303 --> 00:20:41.534
Where were you?! I was lonely!

00:20:41.673 --> 00:20:44.267
I was really lonely!

00:20:44.576 --> 00:20:45.177
Millie...

00:20:45.177 --> 00:20:47.112
Why did you go?! Why?!

00:20:47.112 --> 00:20:50.048
Don't leave me alone! I can't take any more!

00:20:50.048 --> 00:20:52.915
You're the only one Millie's got!

00:20:53.318 --> 00:20:56.989
You're the only one Millie has now...

00:20:56.989 --> 00:20:58.047
Millie...

00:20:58.223 --> 00:21:00.623
Millie, I'm sorry.

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:02.688
I'm sorry.

00:21:05.163 --> 00:21:06.960
Millie had been holding it in.

00:21:07.899 --> 00:21:09.835
This little girl had never looked away...

00:21:09.835 --> 00:21:13.327
...from the painful reality
that was her father's death...

00:21:13.639 --> 00:21:15.231
...and desperately tried to hold it all in.

00:21:16.341 --> 00:21:19.174
Honoka could not help but hold her close.

00:21:19.745 --> 00:21:22.873
And she could not help but feel happy.

00:21:23.949 --> 00:21:25.416
To Honoka as well,

00:21:26.051 --> 00:21:29.953
Millie was a precious and irreplaceable presence.

00:21:30.989 --> 00:21:32.257
It's pretty.

00:21:32.257 --> 00:21:33.759
Thank you, Hono.

00:21:33.759 --> 00:21:36.261
But next time, Millie wants to go see it with you.

00:21:36.261 --> 00:21:37.956
Sure, let's do that.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:48.006
A flexible civilization...
Juunan na bunmei wa

00:21:48.006 --> 00:21:50.509
...is always rapidly advancing.
Itsudatte nisshin-geppo

00:21:50.509 --> 00:21:53.478
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:57.278
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:22:02.788 --> 00:22:05.757
I realized for the first time...
Hajimete kizuitan da

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:09.454
...with that line, resembling a surprise attack.
Fui-uchi ni nita sono serifu de

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:17.436
My sixth sense was pried open.
Kojiakerareta dai-rokkan

00:22:17.436 --> 00:22:21.463
I'd been waiting for this feeling this whole time.
Kono kankaku o zutto matteita

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:28.447
Opening my heart, just opening it...
Kokoro o hiraite tada hiraite

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:31.416
I embrace the voices of strangers.
Daisansha no koe ukeireru

00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:34.286
Earnestly persevering, just persevering...
Hitasura koraete tada koraete

00:22:34.286 --> 00:22:37.380
I even try turning pages of criticism.
Hinan no peeji mo aketemiru

00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:40.659
I'm going to leave my...
Toushindai no boku wa

00:22:40.659 --> 00:22:43.595
...true-to-life self behind, right here.
Koko ni oite iku yo

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:47.432
You can say whatever you want now...
Mou nanto itte kuretemo

00:22:47.432 --> 00:22:48.956
...and I'm fine with that.
Kekkou da

00:22:49.468 --> 00:22:54.940
Ah, how simple is the impulse to evolve.
Aa nante tanjun da shinka shitai to iu shoudou

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.843
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:22:57.843 --> 00:23:01.040
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.889
Preview

00:23:18.764 --> 00:23:20.129
Blue Breaker!

00:23:20.532 --> 00:23:22.090
This time, I'm going to defeat him!

00:23:22.267 --> 00:23:23.928
I'm going to avenge Pops!

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:28.001
But having gone out there in the PSP,

00:23:28.273 --> 00:23:30.503
I couldn't get into my usual
rhythm for some reason.

00:23:31.109 --> 00:23:33.270
And then the PSP got damaged...

00:23:33.645 --> 00:23:35.613
...and I heard Millie cry out...

00:23:36.948 --> 00:23:40.145
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.285 --> 00:23:42.053
episode 6, "The Wind That Sweeps The Land".

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:43.188
The Wind That Sweeps The Land
episode 6, "The Wind That Sweeps The Land".

00:23:43.188 --> 00:23:44.917
The Wind That Sweeps The Land
